AR3-11 condition 2 puts in HOST_DEFAULT_MAP scope everything that neither the plan, nor the writer constants, nor the I-52 authority determines. A created layer's record other than Name and Color is in that scope, because LayerHelper.cs:25 sets only `Name` and `Color`. AR3-11 condition 1 allows only the three named HDM-CHAR scenarios as sources, and none of their mirrors creates a layer: the FX-1F mirror draws no text or dimension, and the FX-ANN and FX-DIM templates already hold their layers (verified: the only label emitters are SFB:329/338/344 and SPB:334/341, and LHD:258-270 and :356 create layers only when needed). AR3-15, in the same ruling, makes CL-CLEAN-FXANNBLANK-FP a governing clean scenario. V2.1 10.2 requires an expected digest for every sealed element before Commit(), and AR3-11 condition 4 makes the missing fields UNKNOWN (O5). Without a source, the scenario AR3-15 created can never reach O3, which defeats the purpose of AR3-15.
The other candidate sources are not admissible:
- EV-L-OC-LAYER is a governing learning run that records events, not attributes, and AR3-11 forbids governing outputs as a source;
- the RACKCAD_ANOTACIONES record of the FX-ANN fixture instance is host work outside a sealed characterization scenario, and its session context is uncontrolled;
- dropping the fields from the comparison would contradict V2.1 11.1, which lists the layer record fields: colour, linetype, lineweight, on/off, frozen, locked, plot flag, transparency.
A dedicated fourth scenario is the only answer consistent with both AR3-11 and AR3-15. Until ruled, AQ-V4-07 blocks the seal of the BA-04 catalog through C-3b and the BA-08 candidate through K-6.

